# /etc/default/prometheus — systemd EnvironmentFile for the prometheus.service
# unit (Debian package owns this path; we re-install it from the fleet-ops
# MANIFEST so the retention value is version-controlled and survives apt
# upgrades).
#
# fleet-ops#1235: extend the live retention to 40d so the fleet-ops#1151
# baseline-delta job can pull a trailing 4-week window (this week + 4 prior
# weeks ≈ 35d of samples). 40d is 35d + 5d of safety margin so a one-day
# hiccup in the deploy loop does not push the baseline window off the end.
#
# Disk headroom: as of 2026-08-27 the TSDB is ~61M for 15d, so 40d projects
# to <200M. The / partition has >200G free. The headroom guard lives in
# bin/fleet-ops-deploy: before it restarts prometheus to apply a changed
# retention it checks free space on the TSDB filesystem and fails loud
# below the PROM_RETENTION_HEADROOM_GB threshold (default 2G).
#
# Restart required: --storage.tsdb.retention.time is a start-time flag and
# is not picked up on HUP. bin/fleet-ops-deploy detects when this file
# changed and runs `systemctl restart prometheus` instead of a reload;
# unchanged deploys still HUP for rule_files / config reloads. AM and
# node-exporter are independent units and keep scraping across the restart.
ARGS="--config.file=/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml --storage.tsdb.retention.time=40d --web.listen-address=127.0.0.1:9090"
